    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p31-q8-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "$P(x)=x^3-2x^2-5x+6$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$P(x)=(x-3)(x-1)(x+2)$",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}P(1)&=1-2-5+6\\\\P(1)&=0\\end{align*}$$\nHence $x-1$ is a factor. Long division gives quotient $x^2-x-6$ and remainder $0$:\n$$\\begin{align*}x^3-2x^2-5x+6-x^2(x-1)&=-x^2-5x+6\\\\-x^2-5x+6-(-x)(x-1)&=-6x+6\\\\-6x+6-(-6)(x-1)&=0\\end{align*}$$\n$$\\begin{align*}P(x)&=(x-1)(x^2-x-6)\\\\P(x)&=(x-1)(x-3)(x+2)\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 75
      },
      {
        "id": "p31-q8-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$P(x)=2x^3+7x^2-7x-12$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$P(x)=(x+4)(x+1)(2x-3)$",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}P(-1)&=-2+7+7-12\\\\P(-1)&=0\\end{align*}$$\nHence $x+1$ is a factor. Long division gives quotient $2x^2+5x-12$ and remainder $0$:\n$$\\begin{align*}2x^3+7x^2-7x-12-2x^2(x+1)&=5x^2-7x-12\\\\5x^2-7x-12-5x(x+1)&=-12x-12\\\\-12x-12-(-12)(x+1)&=0\\end{align*}$$\n$$\\begin{align*}2x^2+5x-12&=2x^2+8x-3x-12\\\\2x^2+5x-12&=2x(x+4)-3(x+4)\\\\2x^2+5x-12&=(x+4)(2x-3)\\\\P(x)&=(x+1)(x+4)(2x-3)\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 95
      },
      {
        "id": "p31-q8-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "$P(x)=2x^3+3x^2-17x+12$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$P(x)=(x-1)(x+4)(2x-3)$",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}P(1)&=2+3-17+12\\\\P(1)&=0\\end{align*}$$\nHence $x-1$ is a factor. Long division gives quotient $2x^2+5x-12$ and remainder $0$:\n$$\\begin{align*}2x^3+3x^2-17x+12-2x^2(x-1)&=5x^2-17x+12\\\\5x^2-17x+12-5x(x-1)&=-12x+12\\\\-12x+12-(-12)(x-1)&=0\\end{align*}$$\n$$\\begin{align*}2x^2+5x-12&=2x^2+8x-3x-12\\\\2x^2+5x-12&=2x(x+4)-3(x+4)\\\\2x^2+5x-12&=(x+4)(2x-3)\\\\P(x)&=(x-1)(x+4)(2x-3)\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 95
      },
      {
        "id": "p31-q8-d",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "$P(x)=6x^3-5x^2-17x+6$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$P(x)=(2x+3)(x-2)(3x-1)$",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}P(2)&=48-20-34+6\\\\P(2)&=0\\end{align*}$$\nHence $x-2$ is a factor. Long division gives quotient $6x^2+7x-3$ and remainder $0$:\n$$\\begin{align*}6x^3-5x^2-17x+6-6x^2(x-2)&=7x^2-17x+6\\\\7x^2-17x+6-7x(x-2)&=-3x+6\\\\-3x+6-(-3)(x-2)&=0\\end{align*}$$\n$$\\begin{align*}6x^2+7x-3&=6x^2+9x-2x-3\\\\6x^2+7x-3&=3x(2x+3)-(2x+3)\\\\6x^2+7x-3&=(2x+3)(3x-1)\\\\P(x)&=(x-2)(2x+3)(3x-1)\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 95
      }
    ]
